# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
version: "0.1.0~alpha1"
synopsis: "Lwt transport for ocaml-mpc, functorised over Mirage_flow.S"
description: """
The transport layer for ocaml-mpc: length-prefixed framing, a flow-generic
transport, and a driver that owns the clock and turns the sans-IO protocol core
into a running participant.

Functorised over Mirage_flow.S rather than bound to a socket API, so the same
code runs over TCP, over vsock, or over TLS inside a MirageOS/Solo5 unikernel.
It does not depend on unix; mpc-unix does that, and only that.

Lwt rather than Eio is a constraint, not a preference: MirageOS has no Eio
backend, so a unikernel-capable transport has to be Lwt-based."""
maintainer: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
authors: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
license: "ISC"
tags: ["mpc" "threshold-signatures" "frost" "mirage" "org:mirage"]
homepage: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-mpc"
doc: "https://reuna-labs.github.io/ocaml-mpc/"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-mpc/issues"
depends: [
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14.0"}
  "dune" {>= "3.6" & >= "3.6"}
  "mpc" {= version}
  "lwt" {>= "5.6.0"}
  "cstruct" {>= "6.0.0"}
  "mirage-flow" {>= "4.0.0"}
  "mirage-crypto" {>= "2.1.0"}
  "mirage-crypto-rng" {with-test & >= "2.1.0"}
  "mirage-crypto-rng-mirage" {with-test}
  "logs"
  "fmt"
  "alcotest" {with-test}
  "odoc" {with-doc}
]
build: [
  ["dune" "subst"] {dev}
  [
    "dune"
    "build"
    "-p"
    name
    "-j"
    jobs
    "@install"
    "@runtest" {with-test}
    "@doc" {with-doc}
  ]
]
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-mpc.git"
